# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# What must NOT be uploaded to Vercel
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# EVERY FILE UNDER api/ BECOMES A PUBLIC SERVERLESS FUNCTION.
#
# That is Vercel's zero-config rule, and it does not care what the file is
# for: `api/seb-verify.test.js` would be deployed and routed at
# /api/seb-verify.test, reachable by anyone, on the same domain as the
# endpoint that mints SEB proofs. It would not do anything useful — its
# imports are test-only — but a public endpoint nobody meant to ship is
# exactly the kind of surface this repo's audit exists to prevent.
#
# So the probes stay next to the code they test, where they get read and
# maintained, and are excluded here instead of being moved somewhere less
# useful. vitest still finds them: vitest.config.ts includes api/**.
#
# If a second handler ever gets a probe, this pattern already covers it.
api/**/*.test.js
api/**/*.spec.js
